   "id": "root",
   "x": 293,
   "y": 10,
   "w": 760,
   "kind": "dark",
   "title": "Radiation: to CURE or to PALLIATE, and which TOXICITY do I watch for, and WHEN?",
   "lines": [
    "damages DNA in normal and cancer cells alike → split into daily FRACTIONS (standard 1.8–2 Gy) so normal tissue repairs between them",
    "every tissue has a TOLERANCE dose: spinal cord, bowel, kidney and lung often limit it · fast-growing tumours respond soonest"
   ]
  },
